The same daemon process serves the rows written while it was away, including the table added by ALTER CLUSTER ADD
––– input –––
kill -0 $P3 && echo alive; for t in t0 t1; do echo "$t $(mysql -h0 -P3306 -N -e "SELECT id FROM $t" | grep -Eo "[0-9]+" | sort -n | xargs)"; done
––– output –––
alive
t0 1 2
t1 1 2
––– comment –––
Evidence from the node 3 log: IST refused on the files seqno, one rejoin attempt, full SST from the donor position, no crash and no restart
––– input –––
L=/var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log; chk() { grep -q -- "$2" $L && echo "yes: $1" || echo "no: $1"; }; chk 'IST chosen' 'State gap can be likely serviced using IST'; chk 'IST refused on files seqno' "files seqno 1 differs from donor files seqno 3 on IST"; chk 'rejoin attempt 1' "rejoin by SST, attempt 1 of 2"; chk 'SST join sync seqno 5' "join sync 'v1', gtid [^ ]*:5, files seqno 3, sent ok, tables 2, ist 0"; grep -c 'CRASH DUMP' $L; grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok' $L
––– output –––
yes: IST chosen
yes: IST refused on files seqno
yes: rejoin attempt 1
yes: SST join sync seqno 5
0
1
